adit on Kernel

🔥 Adit is an experimental, Vantom-based optimized kernel designed specifically for Redmi Note 10 Pro/Pro Max devices (sweet & sweetin). It prioritizes power efficiency, gaming performance, and system stability without compromising essential features.

🔧 Key Features:

Base Kernel: Vantom (clean & stable)

Step Charging: Multi-step charging based on temperature and battery percentage; supports up to 33W (4.5A current) while ensuring safety and battery longevity

Dual Charger Support: BQ25970 & LN8000, safely configured with active thermal protection

UFS Devfreq Optimization: Efficient scaling with tuned sched governor, timeouts, and clock gating; drastically reduced power consumption

Full PM & CPUFreq Support: Defaults to the *schedutil* governor to balance performance and efficiency

JEITA Thermal Profiling: Adaptive thermal control to maintain safe charging conditions

Idle-Friendly: SPM & RPM level tuning and active runtime PM to maximize efficiency during inactivity

MIUI & AOSP Compatibility: A versatile kernel that performs well in both ecosystems


⚙️ Primary Objectives:

Deliver high performance when needed

Minimize idle and background power consumption

Maintain safe temperature and current limits


📦 Device Support:

sweetin (Redmi Note 10 Pro India)

sweet (Redmi Note 10 Pro Global)
